# What the build context carries. Every service that runs this image bind-mounts
# the repository over /usr/src/app, so the baked copy is never read on this host
# — it exists only for a container started without that mount. Anything here is
# therefore either too large to bake, or something that must never be baked.
#
# Without this file the context was 44.8 GB and `COPY . .` plus the `chown -R`
# after it wrote that twice, which is 89.6 GB of a 93 GB image: a Telegram
# relay carrying the training sets, every mind's harness sessions, and the
# root `.env`.

# Harness and tooling caches
**/__pycache__
*.py[cod]
**/.mypy_cache
**/.pytest_cache
**/.ruff_cache
**/node_modules
**/.vscode
.vscode/

# Interpreters. A materialised venv in an image is a venv built for the host's
# libc, and /opt/venv is the one this image actually runs.
.venv/
venv/
.devvenv/
.pylibs/
.npm_packages/
.local/

# Secrets. The image holds no credential; every service is handed its own
# through the environment and the keyring mount.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# Bulk state, all of it bind-mounted at runtime. data/ is 34 GB, almost all of
# it data/training_sets.
data/
backups/
nervous-system/
img/
.obsidian/
.tmp_sshprobe/
*.log

# Per-mind harness homes: sessions, transcripts and harness credentials, each
# mounted per mind by that mind's own compose fragment.
minds/*/.claude/
minds/*/.codex/
minds/*/.dsh/

# History
.git
